{#- Logomark, built so the guy can move like a marionette (src/assets/js/site.js). Hand-written:
    brand/logomark.svg is generated by scripts/brand.mjs, this file is not. Keep the shapes in sync if the mark changes.

    The original mark is one shape: green pieces with the guy as the empty space between them. Here the
    green is the plain shield outline and the guy is cut out of it with masks:
      guy  = shield outline minus the original pieces (exactly the old empty space), minus the strings, plus
             thin strips inside the strings where the arms and hand tips meet them; one even-odd path, so
             shapes that share an edge leave no hairline seam when the parts move
      cut  = everything, minus the strings (they stay put), minus the guy's parts
    The guy is split into parts (clip paths, overlapping a little at the joints), each in a group the
    script rotates around its joint:
      body (torso and arms, around the chest) > head (around the neck), legs (skewed from the crotch line,
      so the hips and the crotch stay joined while the feet swing)
    The strings stay put, down to their tips under the hands: the arms and hand tips slide along them as the
    body swings (thin strips inside the strings, moving with the body, keep them joined).
    At rest everything is in place, so it looks exactly like the original mark.
    Set `lid` before including, so two logos on one page don't share ids. -#}
